
✅ PROGRAM 1: Configure IP Routing Using RIP
Aim:
To configure IP routing using RIP protocol between routers.
Topology:
2 Routers connected with 2 LAN networks.
IP Addressing:
Device
Interface
IP Address
R1
Fa0/0
192.168.1.1
R1
S0/0/0
10.0.0.1
R2
Fa0/0
192.168.2.1
R2
S0/0/0
10.0.0.2
Steps:
Step 1: Configure IP on R1
Copy code

enable
configure terminal
interface fa0/0
ip address 192.168.1.1 255.255.255.0
no shutdown
exit

interface s0/0/0
ip address 10.0.0.1 255.0.0.0
no shutdown
exit
Step 2: Configure RIP on R1
Copy code

router rip
version 2
network 192.168.1.0
network 10.0.0.0
exit
Step 3: Configure R2 similarly
Copy code

enable
configure terminal
interface fa0/0
ip address 192.168.2.1 255.255.255.0
no shutdown
exit

interface s0/0/0
ip address 10.0.0.2 255.0.0.0
no shutdown
exit

router rip
version 2
network 192.168.2.0
network 10.0.0.0
exit
Step 4: Verification
Copy code

show ip route
ping 192.168.1.1


✅ PROGRAM 2: Configuring Simple & Multi-Area OSPF
Aim:
To configure OSPF routing protocol.
Simple OSPF (Single Area)
On Router:
Copy code

router ospf 1
network 192.168.1.0 0.0.0.255 area 0
network 10.0.0.0 0.255.255.255 area 0
Multi Area OSPF Example
Router 1 (Area 0)
Copy code

router ospf 1
network 192.168.1.0 0.0.0.255 area 0
Router 2 (Area 1)
Copy code

router ospf 1
network 192.168.2.0 0.0.0.255 area 1
Verification
Copy code

show ip ospf neighbor
show ip route


✅ PROGRAM 3: Configuration & Implementation of DHCP Server
Aim:
To configure DHCP server in Linux.
Steps:
Step 1: Install DHCP
Copy code

sudo apt install isc-dhcp-server
Step 2: Edit config file
Copy code

sudo nano /etc/dhcp/dhcpd.conf
Add:
Copy code

subnet 192.168.1.0 netmask 255.255.255.0 {
 range 192.168.1.100 192.168.1.200;
 option routers 192.168.1.1;
 option domain-name-servers 8.8.8.8;
}
Step 3: Start Service
Copy code

sudo systemctl start isc-dhcp-server
sudo systemctl enable isc-dhcp-server


